  "footnote": "Minimum 12 major courses, each with C- or better. Cross-listed registration counts: use the corresponding LSP code in this checklist because the page lists no equivalent codes; otherwise a cross-listing may be refused or counted toward the outside-elective limit. The page provides no independent-study or thesis course codes; mark approved repeated courses repeatable in the plan. To declare, submit the major application; the Director of Undergraduate Studies assigns a faculty advisor in consultation with the student. Optional honors requires a 3.5 major GPA and 3.0 overall GPA: request admission by May 1 of junior year with a topic and willing LSP faculty advisor, begin summer research if approved, and enroll in thesis hours both senior semesters. The advisor and a second reader evaluate the thesis.",
